    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\r\n\r\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\r\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\r\n\r\n### Module(s)\r\n\r\nmini.pick\r\n\r\n### Description\r\n\r\nIt would be nice if we could have side previews in pickers as opposed to the Tab ones. Not actually for an aesthetic reason, but because it's useful to preview as we're scrolling through several files. Making it easier to find what we're looking for.",
